-*   AABB maximum corner $\mathbf{max} = (max_x, max_y, max_z)$
-*   Optional: Ray clipping range $[t_{clip\_min}, t_{clip\_max}]$
+*   Ray direction $\mathbf{d} = (d_x, d_y, d_z)$ (assumed non-zero for standard implementation; see pitfalls)
+*   AABB minimum corner $\mathbf{b}_{min} = (b_{min,x}, b_{min,y}, b_{min,z})$
+*   AABB maximum corner $\mathbf{b}_{max} = (b_{max,x}, b_{max,y}, b_{max,z})$
 
 **Outputs:**
-*   Intersection interval $[t_{near}, t_{far}]$
-*   Boolean hit status
+*   Boolean `hit`: true if intersection exists.
+*   Float `t_near`: parametric distance to entry.
+*   Float `t_far`: parametric distance to exit.
+*   (Optional) Intersection point $\mathbf{p} = \mathbf{o} + t_{near}\mathbf{d}$ and normal $\mathbf{n}$ [S1, unofficial].
 
